# RFQ subscriber
#
# Shows:   the market side asking to be sent RFQs — `rfq request` in a `run` block, `answered`
#          for each RFQ it draws, `unsubscribe`, and `on sent rfq request` minding one
#          sent by hand
# Needs:   a FIX 4.3 or later session: run it on LOOP-MKT with rfq-responder armed on LOOP-CLI,
#          both edited to FIX.4.4
# Watch:   Sent RFQ Requests (Market menu): Active, the RFQs column counting, then
#          Unsubscribed; Received RFQs for the RFQs themselves
# Outcome: a subscription for IBM and MSFT for a minute, then an unsubscribe that says how
#          many RFQs it drew; one sent by hand is ended after five minutes

run
    when answered
        log 'RFQ ${rfq_request.last_quote_req_id}, ${rfq_request.quote_requests} so far'
    rfq request symbols: 'IBM; MSFT', subscription: subscribe, request_type: automatic
    after 60s
    let drawn = rfq_request.quote_requests
    unsubscribe
    pass '${drawn} RFQs for ${rfq_request.symbols}'

on sent rfq request
    after 5m
    if rfq_request.status == 'Active'
        unsubscribe
